design/bom.csv:52:"Cell, curved",BT1,1,"custom curved cell in the band, 4.35 V; from +48.7 degrees through the bottom to -98.0 degrees at US 9 (inside model v4, architecture 17.15)",Grepow (custom order),,curved pouch,1.6 x 6.0 x 39.36 on its centre line at US 9,20 to 27 mAh at US 9 (18.2 to 24.3 mAh at US 7),"377.9 cubic mm x 0.054 to 0.072 mAh per cubic mm = 20.4 to 27.2 mAh (architecture 17.15); 4.35 V; charge 15 mA (0.55 to 0.74 C) with the nPM1304 until Grepow states its own limit (architecture 17.13, S12); the motor draws up to 175 mA at each start (17.16); shorter per smaller ring size, not re-measured per size (thin-notes.md K9); by ring size 18.2 to 24.3 mAh at US 7 up to 24.7 to 32.9 mAh at US 13, smallest 18.2 mAh at US 7 (architecture 17.17)",CALC,"design/architecture.md sections 17.13, 17.15, 17.16 (S12) ; design/mech/thin/thin-notes.md section Model v4 ; design/architecture.md 17.17",,"S12: Grepow must answer: can it build the curved cell 1.6 x 6.0 x 39.36 mm on its centre line (17.15) at 4.35 V, its order code, price, the highest charge current it accepts (the nPM1304 sets 4 to 100 mA) and the discharge current the cell and its protection circuit allow (motor start 175 mA, 17.16)"
