design/firmware-evidence/f5/new_8_1_to_8_5.md:37:2. **`CHARGE_CURRENT` is one named constant**, set in one place, in microamps: 15,000. A build fails to compile when it is unset, above 18,200 (1 C of the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh, architecture 17.17), under 4,000 or over 100,000, or not a multiple of 500 [NPM p24]. The firmware disables the charger before it writes the current register and enables it after [NPM p24: "CHARGER must be disabled before changing the current setting in register BCHGISET"].
