design/firmware-evidence/f5/new_8_1_to_8_5.md:99:Recording current: architecture 17.15 and 17.17 use 4.0 mA, which counts the old microphones at 2 x 0.58 mA; the SPK0641HT4H-1 draws 0.63 mA at 1.8 V [DS line 97], so F5 uses 4.0 + 2 x (0.63 - 0.58) = 4.1 mA. This counts the 0.10 mA rise as if drawn from the cell, an over-count: through the 1.8 V rail it is 2 x 0.05 x 1.8 / (3.8 x 0.9) = 0.05 mA from the cell [CALC]. Recording hours: 18.2 / 4.1 = 4.44 and 32.9 / 4.1 = 8.02. At 13 mA: 18.2 / 13 = 1.40 and 32.9 / 13 = 2.53. Standby at 0.03 mA: 18.2 / 0.03 = 607 hours = 25.3 days and 32.9 / 0.03 = 1,097 hours = 45.7 days. Per ring size at 4.1 mA [CALC, `design/firmware-f5-notes.md`]:
