design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b8_protocol_sentence.md:9:4. **Battery per ring size** (architecture 17.15 and 17.17): the cell is 18.2 to 24.3 mAh at US 7 up to 24.7 to 32.9 mAh at US 13. Minutes of every threshold use the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh; every hours figure is a range across the sizes; every C-rate is recomputed (sections 1.1, 3.1, 8.1, 8.5, H7).
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b8_protocol_sentence.md:107:Battery thresholds (state of charge from the Nordic fuel gauge library, section 8.3, with the motor's charge added; voltage from the nPM1304 system monitor ADC [NPM p99], averaged over 10 s). Recomputed in F5 for the cells of ring sizes US 7 to 13, 18.2 to 32.9 mAh (architecture 17.17), and a recording current of 4.1 mA (section 8.5). A threshold protects a minimum of recording time, so its minutes are given on the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh at US 7 (architecture 17.17: "must use the smallest cell of the smallest size: 18.2 mAh (US 7)"):
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b8_protocol_sentence.md:111:- The percentages stay 15, 5 and 2: they are shares of the cell, so the cell size changes what they mean in time, not their value. Capacity left on the smallest cell [CALC]: B15 2.73 mAh, B5 0.91 mAh, B2 0.36 mAh (18.2 mAh times 15, 5 and 2 %). Time left at 4.1 mA on 18.2 mAh [CALC]: B15 40 min, B5 13 min, B2 5 min. On the largest cell, 32.9 mAh at US 13, the same shares give B15 72 min, B5 24 min, B2 10 min [CALC]. Recording time from full at 4.1 mA: 4.4 to 8.0 hours across US 7 to 13 (section 8.5). The share is the fuel gauge's, whose model of these cells is not verified (section 10.5, item 26).
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b8_protocol_sentence.md:299:- A pulse draws below 80 mA while the motor runs and up to 175 mA at its start, from the cell through U11, outside the power chip's 100 mA battery limit (motor-drive.md). On the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh at US 7, that is 4.4 C running and 9.6 C at the start; on the largest, 32.9 mAh at US 13, 2.4 C and 5.3 C [CALC: 80 / 18.2, 175 / 18.2, 80 / 32.9, 175 / 32.9; architecture 17.16, 17.17]; whether the cell and its protection circuit allow it is hardware issue H7.
