design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b4_battery_range.md:898:- First charge of step 26 **[PROPOSED by assembly step 26]**: the charger runs at `CHARGE_CURRENT`, 15 mA, to 4.35 V; the jig reads GET_BATTERY until the state of charge reaches 50 percent (500 in `soc_percent_x10`), then goes to step 27. From an empty cell that takes about 0.61 to 1.10 hours across US 7 to 13 [CALC: 0.5 x 18.2 / 15 and 0.5 x 32.9 / 15]. The cell's maker may set another storage level (S12); the reading depends on the battery model (section 10.5, item 4).
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b4_battery_range.md:1003:26. The fuel-gauge battery model for the curved cells of 18.2 to 32.9 mAh, the accuracy of its state of charge at 4.1 mA with the motor's charge added, and the cell's discharge limit against the motor start of 175 mA (hardware issue H7). Who answers: the cell maker (S12), then the bench.
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b4_battery_range.md:1030:| H7 | The motor draws below 80 mA running and up to 175 mA at each start (architecture 17.16), now straight from the cell through U11 (17.22): 4.4 C running and 9.6 C at the start on the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh, and 2.4 C and 5.3 C on the largest, 32.9 mAh [CALC, section 3.1]. A start takes up to 228 mA from the cell with every other load on (17.22). No cell discharge limit and no protection-circuit trip current is on file. | open | the patterns are unchanged; B15 and B5 stop recording before the cell is low, but a trip of the protection circuit in a motor start would cut power in a pulse | cell maker (Grepow), through open item S12: maximum pulse current of the cell and its protection circuit |
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:9:4. **Battery per ring size** (architecture 17.15 and 17.17): the cell is 18.2 to 24.3 mAh at US 7 up to 24.7 to 32.9 mAh at US 13. Minutes of every threshold use the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh; every hours figure is a range across the sizes; every C-rate is recomputed (sections 1.1, 3.1, 8.1, 8.5, H7).
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:107:Battery thresholds (state of charge from the Nordic fuel gauge library, section 8.3, with the motor's charge added; voltage from the nPM1304 system monitor ADC [NPM p99], averaged over 10 s). Recomputed in F5 for the cells of ring sizes US 7 to 13, 18.2 to 32.9 mAh (architecture 17.17), and a recording current of 4.1 mA (section 8.5). A threshold protects a minimum of recording time, so its minutes are given on the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh at US 7 (architecture 17.17: "must use the smallest cell of the smallest size: 18.2 mAh (US 7)"):
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:111:- The percentages stay 15, 5 and 2: they are shares of the cell, so the cell size changes what they mean in time, not their value. Capacity left on the smallest cell [CALC]: B15 2.73 mAh, B5 0.91 mAh, B2 0.36 mAh (18.2 mAh times 15, 5 and 2 %). Time left at 4.1 mA on 18.2 mAh [CALC]: B15 40 min, B5 13 min, B2 5 min. On the largest cell, 32.9 mAh at US 13, the same shares give B15 72 min, B5 24 min, B2 10 min [CALC]. Recording time from full at 4.1 mA: 4.4 to 8.0 hours across US 7 to 13 (section 8.5). The share is the fuel gauge's, whose model of these cells is not verified (section 10.5, item 26).
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:299:- A pulse draws below 80 mA while the motor runs and up to 175 mA at its start, from the cell through U11, outside the power chip's 100 mA battery limit (motor-drive.md). On the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh at US 7, that is 4.4 C running and 9.6 C at the start; on the largest, 32.9 mAh at US 13, 2.4 C and 5.3 C [CALC: 80 / 18.2, 175 / 18.2, 80 / 32.9, 175 / 32.9; architecture 17.16, 17.17]; whether the cell and its protection circuit allow it is hardware issue H7.
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:724:| | `current-microamp` | `CHARGE_CURRENT` = 15,000 (15 mA, architecture 17.13: 1 C of the smallest cell of the range, kept until the cell's maker states its own limit, open item S12). The chip takes 4 to 100 mA in 0.5 mA steps [NPM p24, p29]. On the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh (US 7), 15 mA is 0.82 C; on the largest, 32.9 mAh (US 13), 0.46 C [CALC: 15 / 18.2, 15 / 32.9]. With the chip's accuracy of plus or minus 10 % [NPM p29] the current is 13.5 to 16.5 mA, at most 0.91 C on 18.2 mAh [CALC: 16.5 / 18.2] | [SRC 17] |
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:740:2. **`CHARGE_CURRENT` is one named constant**, set in one place, in microamps: 15,000. A build fails to compile when it is unset, above 18,200 (1 C of the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh, architecture 17.17), under 4,000 or over 100,000, or not a multiple of 500 [NPM p24]. The firmware disables the charger before it writes the current register and enables it after [NPM p24: "CHARGER must be disabled before changing the current setting in register BCHGISET"].
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:745:| US 7 | 18.2 to 24.3 mAh | 1.21 to 1.62 hours |
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:751:| US 13 | 24.7 to 32.9 mAh | 1.65 to 2.19 hours |
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:798:| Hours on the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh at US 7 [CALC] | 4.4 | 607 (25.3 days) |
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:799:| Hours across US 7 to 13, 18.2 to 32.9 mAh [CALC] | 4.4 to 8.0 | 607 to 1,097 (25.3 to 45.7 days) |
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:800:| Hours at a Plaud's 13 mA, 18.2 to 32.9 mAh [CALC] | 1.4 to 2.5 | |
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken/b2_motor_q1.md:802:Recording current: architecture 17.15 and 17.17 use 4.0 mA, which counts the old microphones at 2 x 0.58 mA; the SPK0641HT4H-1 draws 0.63 mA at 1.8 V [DS line 97], so F5 uses 4.0 + 2 x (0.63 - 0.58) = 4.1 mA. This counts the 0.10 mA rise as if drawn from the cell, an over-count: through the 1.8 V rail it is 2 x 0.05 x 1.8 / (3.8 x 0.9) = 0.05 mA from the cell [CALC]. Recording hours: 18.2 / 4.1 = 4.44 and 32.9 / 4.1 = 8.02. At 13 mA: 18.2 / 13 = 1.40 and 32.9 / 13 = 2.53. Standby at 0.03 mA: 18.2 / 0.03 = 607 hours = 25.3 days and 32.9 / 0.03 = 1,097 hours = 45.7 days. Per ring size at 4.1 mA [CALC, `design/firmware-f5-notes.md`]:
