design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken_final/b7_power_chip_name.md:898:- First charge of step 26 **[PROPOSED by assembly step 26]**: the charger runs at `CHARGE_CURRENT`, 15 mA, to 4.35 V; the jig reads GET_BATTERY until the state of charge reaches 50 percent (500 in `soc_percent_x10`), then goes to step 27. From an empty cell that takes about 0.61 to 1.10 hours across US 7 to 13 [CALC: 0.5 x 18.2 / 15 and 0.5 x 32.9 / 15]. The cell's maker may set another storage level (S12); the reading depends on the battery model (section 10.5, item 4).
