design/firmware-evidence/f6/broken/b10_gain_minus11.md:8:3. **Charge**: `CHARGE_CURRENT` stays 15,000 µA, 0.85 C of 17.6 mAh; the compile limit (1 C of the smallest cell) becomes 17,600 µA (before: 18,200); the charge time table follows the measured cells (section 8.1).
design/firmware-evidence/f6/broken/b10_gain_minus11.md:16:4. **Battery per ring size** (architecture 17.15 and 17.17; since F6, 17.26): the measured cell is 17.6 to 23.5 mAh at US 7, 18.9 to 25.3 at US 8, 20.3 to 27.1 at US 9, 21.2 to 28.3 at US 10, 22.1 to 29.5 at US 11, 23.0 to 30.7 at US 12 and 23.9 to 31.9 mAh at US 13 (in F5, before the measurement, the calculated 18.2 to 24.3 up to 24.7 to 32.9 mAh). Minutes of every threshold use the smallest cell, 17.6 mAh (18.2 mAh before F6); every hours figure is a range across the sizes; every C-rate is recomputed (sections 1.1, 3.1, 8.1, 8.5, H7).
design/firmware-evidence/f6/broken/b10_gain_minus11.md:1023:Run: `design/.venv/bin/python -I design/firmware-check.py` (exit 0 = pass, 1 = a rule fails). It reads `design/architecture.md`, `design/ecad/ring/netlist.csv` and the Knowles datasheet copy `design/mech/mic-path/datasheets/knowles-spk0641ht4h-1_chipsmall.txt`. Kept from F2 to F4: sections 1 to 10 present; every state of a transition is in the state list, every listed state has a transition out and, except `SHIP` and `BOOT`, one in, and the number of transition rows equals the number stated under the table; every pin and signal name is in architecture section 7, no spare pin is used, and each signal-pin pair matches; the RAM lines sum to the total, at most 512 KB; the charge voltage equals the cell's type in architecture section 2; each PDM clock line divides 32 MHz by a whole prescaler of 4 to 126, uses a ratio of the chip and gives 16,000 or 8,000 Hz; 64-byte bulk packets at full speed (6.1); the motor marking rule (4.7); the schematic rules for the microphone clock (4.5), the storage lines (5.1) and the screen sequence (3.3); thermistor value and ordered limits (8.1); none of the removed names outside the change lists; VDD_MIC on in exactly one state (1.1) and one power-table row (8.2), the recording state; only a long press starts or stops a recording, a short or double press never changes state, and no direction, button or other event touches the recording state; the gesture, centre-source, warning-pulse, hold-off and collision rules of F4; the audio format and chunk arithmetic; one PDM instance; the joystick switches against architecture 17.3 and the 40 ms rule against 16.5; unused pins only on lines that say unused; four pads in order; every row into `CHARGING` and both ship-exit rows say "charge on", `charging-enable` is on whenever VBUS is present, R-CHG stated; section 8.6 states VBUS is an input only; `questions_for_owner` and the RESULT line. Changed in F5 (each replaces an F4 check that asserted what F5 changes): the header says Version F5, follows A5 sections 17.11 to 17.23 and has the list "Changes from F4 to F5" with 8 items; the removed-name rule runs from that list to "How to read this" and now also bans the older power chip's name, the F3 battery range, the old microphone and datasheet names and the discharge-limit property; `CHARGE_CURRENT` is 15,000 µA in `current-microamp`, a multiple of 500 inside 4,000 to 100,000 and at most 1 C of the smallest cell of architecture 17.17, and T-CHARGE has a pass limit (in F4 both were BLOCKED on S12); the microphone mode range is read from the Knowles datasheet copy (F4 used fixed numbers of the older part), the microphone part name is in 4.1 and 8.5, and the gain is 0 dB, the register 0x28 (2 x 0 + 0x28), the header `gain_code` equal to it, and the stored full scale (94 dB SPL minus the sensitivity read from the Knowles copy) equal to the acoustic overload point read from the same copy; section 3.1 names U11, MOT_EN, VMOT and the 0.55 ms delay and never Q1, and architecture 17.22 names U11 (F4 checked Q1 and full duty on VDD_3V0); the battery minutes of 1.1 and the hours of 8.5 are recomputed from the smallest and largest cells of architecture 17.17 and the recording current 4.0 + 2 x (0.63 - 0.58) mA (F4 checked a single range against architecture 17.10); the ship section 8.4 names TASKENTERSHIPMODE, the VBUS removal and EVENTVBUSREMOVED and no timed hibernate; SHIP_SAMPLE keeps the factory flag in 9.3 and in 1.2; section 7 starts with the protocol sentence. New in F5: every "SIGNAL Pn.nn" pair and every chip pin of firmware.md is checked against the U1 rows of `netlist.csv`, and the power chip, microphone and motor nets this file names (GPIO0 on PMIC_INT, LSOUT1 on VDD_MIC, LSOUT2 on VDD_SD, U5 and U6 SELECT, U11 EN, OUT and IN, R61 and R62) against their netlist rows. Changed in F6: the cells per size are read from the measured table of architecture 17.26 (no longer 17.17); the compile limit of 8.1 must equal 1 C of the smallest cell, 17,600 µA; the header says Version F6 with sections 17.11 to 17.26 and the list "Changes from F5 to F6" has 4 items; and no line outside the change lists may name 18.2, 24.3 or 32.9 or 18,200, the values of the calculated cells, unless it holds the word "before". Rules it cannot check (timing values, protocol layouts, the meaning of text) are checked by review.
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken_final/b2_motor_q1.md:9:4. **Battery per ring size** (architecture 17.15 and 17.17): the cell is 18.2 to 24.3 mAh at US 7 up to 24.7 to 32.9 mAh at US 13. Minutes of every threshold use the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh; every hours figure is a range across the sizes; every C-rate is recomputed (sections 1.1, 3.1, 8.1, 8.5, H7).
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken_final/b2_motor_q1.md:107:Battery thresholds (state of charge from the Nordic fuel gauge library, section 8.3, with the motor's charge added; voltage from the nPM1304 system monitor ADC [NPM p99], averaged over 10 s). Recomputed in F5 for the cells of ring sizes US 7 to 13, 18.2 to 32.9 mAh (architecture 17.17), and a recording current of 4.1 mA (section 8.5). A threshold protects a minimum of recording time, so its minutes are given on the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh at US 7 (architecture 17.17: "must use the smallest cell of the smallest size: 18.2 mAh (US 7)"):
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken_final/b2_motor_q1.md:111:- The percentages stay 15, 5 and 2: they are shares of the cell, so the cell size changes what they mean in time, not their value. Capacity left on the smallest cell [CALC]: B15 2.73 mAh, B5 0.91 mAh, B2 0.36 mAh (18.2 mAh times 15, 5 and 2 %). Time left at 4.1 mA on 18.2 mAh [CALC]: B15 40 min, B5 13 min, B2 5 min. On the largest cell, 32.9 mAh at US 13, the same shares give B15 72 min, B5 24 min, B2 10 min [CALC]. Recording time from full at 4.1 mA: 4.4 to 8.0 hours across US 7 to 13 (section 8.5). The share is the fuel gauge's, whose model of these cells is not verified (section 10.5, item 26).
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken_final/b2_motor_q1.md:299:- A pulse draws below 80 mA while the motor runs and up to 175 mA at its start, from the cell through U11, outside the power chip's 100 mA battery limit (motor-drive.md). On the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh at US 7, that is 4.4 C running and 9.6 C at the start; on the largest, 32.9 mAh at US 13, 2.4 C and 5.3 C [CALC: 80 / 18.2, 175 / 18.2, 80 / 32.9, 175 / 32.9; architecture 17.16, 17.17]; whether the cell and its protection circuit allow it is hardware issue H7.
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken_final/b2_motor_q1.md:724:| | `current-microamp` | `CHARGE_CURRENT` = 15,000 (15 mA, architecture 17.13: 1 C of the smallest cell of the range, kept until the cell's maker states its own limit, open item S12). The chip takes 4 to 100 mA in 0.5 mA steps [NPM p24, p29]. On the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh (US 7), 15 mA is 0.82 C; on the largest, 32.9 mAh (US 13), 0.46 C [CALC: 15 / 18.2, 15 / 32.9]. With the chip's accuracy of plus or minus 10 % [NPM p29] the current is 13.5 to 16.5 mA, at most 0.91 C on 18.2 mAh [CALC: 16.5 / 18.2] | [SRC 17] |
design/firmware-evidence/f5/broken_final/b2_motor_q1.md:740:2. **`CHARGE_CURRENT` is one named constant**, set in one place, in microamps: 15,000. A build fails to compile when it is unset, above 18,200 (1 C of the smallest cell, 18.2 mAh, architecture 17.17), under 4,000 or over 100,000, or not a multiple of 500 [NPM p24]. The firmware disables the charger before it writes the current register and enables it after [NPM p24: "CHARGER must be disabled before changing the current setting in register BCHGISET"].
