ed what F5 changes): the header says Version F5, follows A5 sections 17.11 to 17.23 and has the list "Changes from F4 to F5" with 8 items; the removed-name rule runs from that list to "How to read this" and now also bans the older power chip's name, the F3 battery range, the old microphone and datasheet names and the discharge-limit property; `CHARGE_CURRENT` is 15,000 µA in `current-microamp`, a multiple of 500 inside 4,000 to 100,000 and at most 1 C of the smallest cell of architecture 17.17, and T-CHARGE has a pass limit (in F4 both were BLOCKED on S12); the microphone mode range is read from the Knowles datasheet copy (F4 used fixed numbers of the older part), the microphone part name is in 4.1 and 8.5, and the gain is 0 dB, the register 0x28 (2 x 0 + 0x28), the header `gain_code` equal to it, and the stored full scale (94 dB SPL minus the sensitivity read from the Knowles copy) equal to the acoustic overload point read from the same copy; section 3.1 names U11, MOT_EN, VMOT and the 0.55 ms delay and never Q1, and architecture 17.22 names U11 (F4 checked Q1 and full duty on VDD_3V0); the battery minutes of 1.1 and the hours of 8.5 are recomputed from the smallest and largest cells of architecture 17.17 and the recording current 4.0 + 2 x (0.63 - 0.58) mA (F4 checked a single range against architecture 17.10); the ship section 8.4 names TASKENTERSHIPMODE, the VBUS removal and EVENTVBUSREMOVED and no timed hibernate; SHIP_SAMPLE keeps the factory flag in 9.3 and in 1.2; section 7 starts with the protocol sentence. New in F5: every "SIGNAL Pn.nn" pair and every chip pin of firmware.md is checked against the U1 rows of `netlist.csv`, and the power chip, microphone and motor nets this file names (GPIO0 on PMIC_INT, LSOUT1 on VDD_MIC, LSOUT2 on VDD_SD, U5 and U6 SELECT, U11 EN, OUT and IN, R61 and R62) against their netlist rows. Changed in F6: the cells per size are read from the measured table of architecture 17.26 (no longer 17.17); the compile limit of 8.1 must equal 1 C of the smallest cell, 17,600 µA; the header says Version F6 with sections 17.11 to 17.26 and the list "Changes from F5 to F6" has 4 items; and no line outside the change lists may name a value of the calculated cells (18.2, 24.3 or 32.9 mAh, or 18,200 µA) unless the word "before" stands within 60 characters of it. Rules it cannot check (timing values, protocol layouts, the meaning of text) are checked by review.
design/firmware-evidence/f6/broken_run2/b10_gain_minus11.md:6:1. **Measured cells** (17.26): US 7 17.6 to 23.5 mAh up to US 13 23.9 to 31.9 mAh replace the calculated cells of 17.17 (before: 18.2 to 32.9 mAh). The smallest cell is 17.6 mAh (sections 1.1, 3.1, 8.1, 8.5, 9.3, 10.5, H7, H8).
design/firmware-evidence/f6/broken_run2/b10_gain_minus11.md:7:2. **Thresholds on 17.6 mAh**: B15 39 min, B5 13 min, B2 5 min at 4.1 mA (before: 40, 13, 5 min on 18.2 mAh) (section 1.1).
design/firmware-evidence/f6/broken_run2/b10_gain_minus11.md:8:3. **Charge**: `CHARGE_CURRENT` stays 15,000 µA, 0.85 C of 17.6 mAh; the compile limit (1 C of the smallest cell) becomes 17,600 µA (before: 18,200); the charge time table follows the measured cells (section 8.1).
design/firmware-evidence/f6/broken_run2/b10_gain_minus11.md:16:4. **Battery per ring size** (architecture 17.15 and 17.17; since F6, 17.26): the measured cell is 17.6 to 23.5 mAh at US 7, 18.9 to 25.3 at US 8, 20.3 to 27.1 at US 9, 21.2 to 28.3 at US 10, 22.1 to 29.5 at US 11, 23.0 to 30.7 at US 12 and 23.9 to 31.9 mAh at US 13 (in F5, before the measurement, the calculated 18.2 to 24.3 up to 24.7 to 32.9 mAh). Minutes of every threshold use the smallest cell, 17.6 mAh (18.2 mAh before F6); every hours figure is a range across the sizes; every C-rate is recomputed (sections 1.1, 3.1, 8.1, 8.5, H7).
