design/protocol/evidence/v04/ring-link-protocol-v03.md:67:- The ring holds the DESIGN CAPACITY of its cell as a build constant per ring size: the low end of the range of architecture 17.17 for that size (US 7 18.2 mAh, US 8 19.3, US 9 20.4, US 10 21.5, US 11 22.6, US 12 23.6, US 13 24.7). From it the ring derives the threshold in percent: the next whole percent above RESERVE_MAH / design capacity. **US 7:** (0.05 x 18.2 + 4.5) / 18.2 = 5.41 / 18.2 = 29.73 %, so **30 %** (5.46 mAh; 4.55 mAh above B5 = 66.4 minutes at 4.111 mA). **US 13:** (0.05 x 24.7 + 4.5) / 24.7 = 5.735 / 24.7 = 23.22 %, so **24 %** (5.928 mAh; 4.693 mAh above B5 = 68.5 minutes). The other sizes: US 8 29 %, US 9 28 %, US 10 26 %, US 11 25 %, US 12 25 % (calc03.out gives all seven; every one leaves at least 65.9 minutes above B5).
