design/ecad/motor-drive/motor-drive.md:77:- Ship mode: U11 stays on the cell. Its shutdown current is 0.1 uA typical and 1 uA max [TLV755P p5]. At 1 uA alone a 20.4 mAh cell would last 850 days [budget SHIP_DAYS_ON_LDO_ALONE]; in the worst case ship-mode drain grows by up to 3.5 times [budget SHIP_FACTOR; ESTIMATE of 0.4 uA for the nPM1304 alone read off Figure 3, spec p9].
design/ecad/motor-drive/motor-drive.md:78:- Fuel gauge: the nPM1304 measures battery current inside its own path [spec p99]; the motor's charge now bypasses it. Bound: one MF pattern is at most 0.02917 mAh [budget MF_CHARGE_BOUND], and 100 such patterns a day would be 2.917 mAh, 14.3 % of a 20.4 mAh cell [budget MOTOR_MAH_PER_DAY_BOUND, MOTOR_DAY_SHARE_SMALL_CELL; ESTIMATE, a deliberate over-count]. The firmware must add the motor's charge (pulse time x 80 mA, plus a start allowance) to the gauge (change F3 below).
